From 99836057d0022ad3cdd24df838703e10d8feed14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:46:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a 3D video at 30 or 25 pictures a second gets
 the 3D mode at twice that rate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 3D output took a mode only at the refresh rate of the mode that
Kodi chose. A 30p side-by-side (half) or top-and-bottom video plays in
a 1080p30 mode, and HDMI makes no 3D layout mandatory at 1080p30: where
the display has none there, the two halves went out in the 2D mode and
the display was switched to 3D by hand. 3D displays often take
side-by-side (half) and top-and-bottom at 1080p60 and 1080p50.

STEREO::Choose() now looks, only where nothing exists at the rate of
Kodi's mode, for the same at exactly twice that rate (59.94 Hz for
29.97, never 60.000 for it): frame packing, then the mode of the half
layout, then the vendor InfoFrame on nvidia-drm, with the rules of
size and lines that hold at Kodi's rate. Each picture is then shown
twice, one refresh after the other, as Kodi shows any 30p video in a
60 Hz mode; nothing is made between them, and the picture rate stays
what it was. Only where that rate is known and is the refresh rate of
Kodi's mode (one picture a refresh: STEREO::Allowed::pictureRate, the
frame rate of the video that plays); and as Kodi's own choice of a mode
takes a double refresh rate: always without a whitelist of modes, with
one only where its option of double refresh rates is on and the 2D mode
at twice the rate is in it. In every other case the choice is the one
it was: the 2D mode, with the two halves in it.

The output of the resolution at twice its rate keeps what is drawn and
calibrated for the resolution, as the 3D mode of its own timing does;
the log says which mode it is and that each picture is shown twice. The
help of the setting says so, in English and Spanish (the parts that the
change to "tú" and "vos" rewrites are left as they are).

The choice at the rate of Kodi's mode, which is everything that was
chosen before, goes through the statements it went through, now in
DETAIL::ChooseAtRate() with that rate.

Checked on the host: the 3D test with 24 new checks passes (253, with
the sanitizers); against the header from before, the nine checks that
need a doubled rate fail and no other; six mutations of the new rules
each make it fail. WinSystemGbm.cpp compiled (syntax check with the
commands of the build). Not seen on a 3D display, and not run: no 3D
display was at hand.
